    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focusing on high-ceiling leverage, prioritizing speed-game matchups and favorable park factors. Our strongest play of the day is **Isaac Paredes** (72.13), who draws a prime matchup against a struggling Klassen (6.12 xERA); the combination of a massive SP skill advantage (+19%) and a dynamic platoon boost (+9%) makes him our anchor. We are also leaning heavily into our speed threats today, with **Corbin Carroll** (66.31) and **Seiya Suzuki** (62.06) both benefiting from slow opposing pitchers who project to surrender significant stolen base opportunities. **Mickey Moniak** (65.81) also climbs into our \"Strong\" tier due to an elite 14% park boost, though we must monitor the 37% rain risk in his contest, as any delay could dampen his efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was excluding **Vinnie Pasquantino** (43.58). While he is a perennial threat, his dynamic platoon disadvantage against the lefty Basso (3.53 xERA) dragged his daily efficiency score below our threshold, forcing us to roll with **Josh Naylor** (44.49) in the UTIL slot despite his own difficult matchup. We are keeping a close eye on **Griffin Conine** (41.74); his matchup against Wheeler (3.02 xERA) is daunting, but his solid 0.395 xwOBA kept him just above our floor. With **James Wood** still sidelined on the IL and **Cole Young** and **Zach McKinstry** failing to meet our strict 40.0 minimum performance floor, the current construction remains our optimal path to closing the gap in stolen bases and counting stats.",
